            "gitignore works retroactively \u2014 just create the file",
            "Move the files to another folder \u2014 out of sight, out of repo"
          ],
          "evidence": [
            [
              "terminal",
              "$ git status\nmodified:   .env          # contains API keys!\nmodified:   debug.log"
            ]
          ],
          "hint": ".gitignore stops future tracking. But .env is already tracked \u2014 what removes it from the index while keeping the working file?",
          "id": "git-gitignore",
          "mins": 5,
          "objectives": [
            ".gitignore",
            "Untracking"
          ],
          "prompt": "How do you fix this properly?",
          "situation": "Secrets (.env) and logs are being committed; the repo needs them ignored going forward.",
          "title": "Secrets in the repo",
          "why": "Two steps: (1) .gitignore with patterns (*.log, .env, node_modules/, plus !exceptions) stops future tracking; (2) git rm --cached .env removes the already-tracked file from the index while keeping the working copy. gitignore alone never untracks. And the committed secrets must be rotated \u2014 removing them from history (filter-repo/BFG) is a separate, heavier operation, but rotation is non-negotiable."
        },
        {
          "answer": 2,
