          "prompt": "What is the clean sequence?",
          "situation": "A pull --rebase is blocked by uncommitted local changes.",
          "title": "The blocked rebase",
          "why": "git stash push shelves the dirty working tree (with a message) into the stash stack, leaving a clean tree for the pull/rebase; git stash pop restores it afterward (list/show to inspect, drop to discard). Committing half-done work just to pull pollutes history; deleting it destroys work. The stash is the clipboard for uncommitted changes."
