          "title": "The incomplete commit",
          "why": "git commit --amend folds staged changes into the tip commit (replacing it with a new hash). Safe only for unpushed commits \u2014 amending published history rewrites hashes others may have based work on. For pushed mistakes, the rule is: new commits fix old ones (git revert for undoing). Amend = revise private history; revert = correct public history."
